flowdata=[('btc-cash-reporting-and-reconciliation','Cash reporting and reconciliation using Bank Transaction Codes',['cash-account-servicer','cash-account-owner'],'A transaction resulting in a cash movement on the customer account is to be reported. The source sets this scope, but does not name a request message or schedule.','P92–P101; §3.1.1; Word-PDF page 5',[
('1','cash-account-servicer','Reports the transaction using harmonised Bank Transaction Code information.','Account owner as business consumer; transport sender/receiver and exact ISO message not specified.'),('2','cash-account-owner','Uses the reported information for cash management and reconciliation.','No subsequent message is defined.'),('3','cash-account-owner','Reconciles the reason for the cash movement to the sub-ledger and/or routes the information to an adequate customer processing system.','The and/or alternatives are expressly retained.')], 'Reporting supports reconciliation and appropriate processing at the customer side. These are source-stated objectives, not asserted success guarantees.'),('btc-standing-order-processing','Standing-order processing in credit-transfer code definitions',['cash-account-owner','originating-party','cash-account-servicer'],'A party has explicit authority to debit the debtor account. It gives a standing order once, valid for an open or closed period.','T17 row 4; §3.4.2.1; Word-PDF page 25; same definition T27 row 4, page 34',[
('1','cash-account-owner','Either the debit account owner or the originating party, with explicit authority, gives the standing order once.','The account servicer receives the instruction; the source gives no exact message identifier.'),('2','cash-account-servicer','Processes credit transfers at specified intervals during an implicit or explicit period.','Debit-account-owner and originating-party alternatives are mutually alternative source roles, not two required senders.')], 'The order is valid for an open or closed time period. No acknowledgement, termination protocol or completion guarantee is defined by the code description.')]
